.TH aozora-fmt 1  "aozora-fmt 0.4.1 (aozora a53c632 / v0.4.1)" 
.SH NAME
aozora\-fmt \- Idempotent formatter for aozora\-flavored\-markdown
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBaozora\-fmt\fR [\fB\-\-check\fR] [\fB\-w\fR|\fB\-\-write\fR] [\fB\-\-diff\fR] [\fB\-l\fR|\fB\-\-list\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIPATH\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Idempotent formatter for aozora\-flavored\-markdown.
.PP
With no path (or `\-`) it reads stdin and writes the canonical form to stdout. Given files or directories it can check, rewrite, list, or diff them; directories are searched recursively for *.afm, *.aozora, and *.aozora.txt files.
.PP
Exit codes: 0 = success / already formatted, 1 = \-\-check found inputs that would change, 2 = an error occurred.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-check\fR
Verify inputs are already formatted; exit 1 if any would change
.TP
\fB\-w\fR, \fB\-\-write\fR
Rewrite files in place (no\-op when already canonical)
.TP
\fB\-\-diff\fR
Print a unified diff for every file that would change. Implies \-\-check
.TP
\fB\-l\fR, \fB\-\-list\fR
List only the paths that would change (gofmt \-l). Combine with \-w
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit the \-\-check result as machine\-readable JSON. Implies \-\-check
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR [default: auto]
When to colourise \-\-diff output
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto: Colour when stdout is a terminal (honours `NO_COLOR`)
.IP \(bu 2
always: Always colour, even when piped
.IP \(bu 2
never: Never colour
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
[\fIPATH\fR]
Files or directories to format. Use `\-`, or omit, to read stdin
.SH VERSION
v0.4.1 (aozora a53c632 / v0.4.1)
